Agency Background:

Lifeline Connections is a not-for-profit agency that is recognized as a leading behavioral health treatment provider in Washington State, offering a full continuum of care for individuals who have a behavioral health condition. Lifeline Connections' patients receive an unprecedented level of care by highly skilled professionals who know how to help people find and sustain long-term recovery. For over fifty years Lifeline Connections has provided hope, help and healing to thousands of individuals in Washington State and within the Portland, Oregon metro area.

Data System Analyst Posting #20-015

Major Duties:
The Data System Analyst position works under the supervision of the Chief Financial Officer. This position is responsible for developing, producing and delivering regular and ad hoc management information to aid business decision making and to assist in the identification of clinical treatment trends and outcomes.
In fulfilling these duties, the incumbent performs the following duties independently:

• Gathers data from primary or secondary sources, including Electronic Health Records, payroll data, and financial data, and organizes the data into data systems;
• Uses statistical techniques to interpret the results from data and use the information to create reports and support business decision making;
• Utilizes existing databases to optimize the statistical efficiency and quality of data that is worked with;
• Filters and cleans data by reviewing reports and performance indicators to identify and report any keying or coding inaccuracies;
• Reviews data to identify, interpret and report out on any patterns or useful trends in complex data sets;
• Creates new reporting models which combine and summarize data from multiple sources using Excel and other reporting tools;
• Assists with the production and on-going maintenance of detailed, accurate and consistent monthly reporting;
• Other duties as assigned.

Requirements:

• Bachelors Degree in Management Information systems (MIS), Computer Information Systems (CIS), Business Analytics, or related field required;
• Two years experience analyzing data and creating technical, healthcare, and/or financial reports required;
• Advanced Microsoft computer skills, including Excel, Structured Query Language (SQL), Visio Studio and SQL Server Report Manager;
• Ability to produce accurate reports, forms, and other documents;
• Excellent analytical skills;
• Ability to communicate clearly both verbally and in writing;
• Ability to work well with others;
• Prior experience in healthcare data analytics or nonprofit finance and outcome reporting preferred;
• Knowledge of the Washington State behavioral healthcare system desired.

Salary: DOE

Application Process:
Submit a cover letter and resume to Human Resources. We will only accept resumes with a cover letter specifying the position title and posting number of the position you are applying for. For more information on this and other positions, please visit our website at www.lifelineconnections.org

